ter all day at the office, so I\'m not sure if it\'s from that or not.\n\n[doctor] I understand. Have you noticed any difference between your right and left elbow?\n\n[patient] Yes, my right elbow bothers me more than my left. I do most of my typing on the computer, so I\'m not sure if that\'s the cause.\n\n[doctor] Hmm, that\'s interesting. Any other joints that are bothering you?\n\n[patient] No, just the elbows.\n\n[doctor] Okay. Have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your hands?\n\n[patient] Yes, I get occasional numbness and tingling, but it goes away when I shake my arms.\n\n[doctor] Alright, have you had any issues with your toe or any other joints recently?\n\n[patient] Yes, about three months ago, I had an episode of gout in my toe. The medication I was given helped, and I haven\'t had any flare-ups since.\n\n[doctor] Good to hear that the medication helped. Have you been taking it regularly?\n\n[patient] Yes, I\'ve been taking the colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed.\n\n[doctor] That\'s great. How\'s your psoriasis been?\n\n[patient] It\'s under control. I haven\'t had any major issues with it.\n\n[doctor] Excellent. Let\'s go over your systems now. How\'s your neck, respiratory, cardiovascular, and gastrointestinal?\n\n[patient] Everything seems fine.\n\n[doctor] Okay. Any abdominal pain or swelling?\n\n[patient] No, my abdomen is soft.\n\n[doctor] And any swelling or pain in your lower extremities?\n\n[patient] No edema.\n\n[doctor] Great. I\'d like to examine your right elbow now. I\'ll check for any swelling or tenderness. Let\'s start by feeling around the olecranon area. Can you show me your right elbow?\n\n[patient] Sure.\n\n[doctor] Okay, I\'ll gently press here. I can feel some swelling and tenderness around the olecranon. There\'s also some pain when I move your elbow, both pronating and supinating. Flexion and extension cause pain as well.\n\n[patient] Oh, yeah, that hurts.\n\n[doctor] I\'ll also check your left elbow. It looks normal.