ur patella. So your patella\'s inflamed and that\'s causing you some pain. Um, and it\'s probably due to the fact that you\'ve been swimming more and you\'ve been kicking more. Um, and that\'s putting more stress on your patella and that\'s causing it to inflame.\nPatient: OK.\nDoctor: OK, so what I would recommend is that you try to reduce your swimming and reduce your kicking. Um, and if you can, you can try to swim freestyle instead of kicking. Um, and if you can, you can try to stop swimming all together. Um, and if you can\'t stop swimming, then I would recommend that you try to do some straight leg raises. Um, and that will help strengthen your quadriceps and that will help reduce your pain.\nPatient: OK, OK.\nDoctor: OK, and I would also recommend that you take some ibuprofen, um, 600 milligrams four times a day with food. Um, and that will help reduce your pain and inflammation.\nPatient: OK.\nDoctor: OK, and um, are you on any other medications?\nPatient: Um, I\'m on antidepressant medication.\nDoctor: OK, OK, great. Um, and um, are you having any problems with your back?\nPatient: Um, my back\'s been doing well lately.\nDoctor: OK, great. And um, are you having any problems with your hands or wrists?\nPatient: Um, my carpal tunnel\'s been doing well.\nDoctor: OK, great. And um, do you have any other medical problems?\nPatient: Um, no.\nDoctor: OK, great. And um, do you have any other questions?\nPatient: Um, no.\nDoctor: OK, great. Um, OK, so I\'m gonna prescribe you some ibuprofen and I would like you to come back in a couple of weeks and we can check on your knee. Um, and if you have any problems in the meantime, you can call me.\nPatient: OK.\nDoctor: OK, great. And um, is there anything else I can do for you today?\nPatient: No, that\'s all.\nDoctor: OK, great. Well, OK, take care. Bye bye.\nPatient: Bye. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] good morning rebecca , nice to see you .\n[patient] nice to see you too .\n[doctor] so , my nurse told