: Um, I think I\'d like to take them once a day.\nDoctor: Okay. And how long would you like to take them for?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to take them for a month.\nDoctor: Okay. And how about the fiber supplements? What kind of fiber supplements do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some psyllium.\nDoctor: Okay. And how often would you like to take the psyllium?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to take it once a day.\nDoctor: Okay. And how long would you like to take it for?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to take it for a month.\nDoctor: Okay. Alright. So, what else can we do to make your symptoms better?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some stress management techniques. I think we could try some relaxation techniques.\nDoctor: Okay. And what relaxation techniques do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some deep breathing exercises. I think we could try some progressive muscle relaxation.\nDoctor: Okay. And how often would you like to practice the relaxation techniques?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to practice them once a day.\nDoctor: Okay. And how long would you like to practice them for?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to practice them for 10 minutes.\nDoctor: Okay. Alright. So, what else can we do to make your symptoms better?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some probiotics. I think we could try some fiber supplements. I think we could try some dietary changes.\nDoctor: Okay. And what dietary changes do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some low-FODMAP foods. I think we could try some gluten-free foods.\nDoctor: Okay. And what gluten-free foods do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some rice. I think we could try some quinoa.\nDoctor: Okay. And what probiotics do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some probiotics that contain Bifidobacterium and Lactobacillus.\nDoctor: Okay. And how often would you like to take the probiotics?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to take them once a day.\nDoctor: Okay. And how long would you like to take them for?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to take them for a month.\nDoctor: Okay. And how about the fiber supplements? What kind of fiber supplements do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some psyllium.\nDoctor: Okay. And how often would you like to take the psyllium?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to take it once a day.\nDoctor: Okay. And how long would you like to take it for?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to take it for a month.\nDoctor: Okay. Alright. So, what else can we do to make your symptoms better?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some stress management techniques. I think we could try some relaxation techniques.\nDoctor: Okay. And what relaxation techniques do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some deep breathing exercises. I think we could try some progressive muscle relaxation.\nDoctor: Okay. And how often would you like to practice the relaxation techniques?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to practice them once a day.\nDoctor: Okay. And how long would you like to practice them for?\nPatient: Um, I think I\'d like to practice them for 10 minutes.\nDoctor: Okay. Alright. So, what else can we do to make your symptoms better?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some probiotics. I think we could try some fiber supplements. I think we could try some dietary changes.\nDoctor: Okay. And what dietary changes do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some low-FODMAP foods. I think we could try some gluten-free foods.\nDoctor: Okay. And what gluten-free foods do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some rice. I think we could try some quinoa.\nDoctor: Okay. And what probiotics do you think we could try?\nPatient: Um, I think we could try some probiotics that contain Bifidobacterium and Lactobacillus.\nDoctor: Okay. And how often would you like to take the probiotics