's mostly constant.\n\n[doctor]: Alright. Have you noticed any swelling or bruising?\n\n[patient]: Yes, there is some swelling and I can see a big bruise on my elbow.\n\n[doctor]: Hmm, that sounds like it could be a contusion. Let me take a look. (examines the elbow) Yes, you do have some swelling and bruising around the olecranon area. It\'s also tender to the touch and you have limited range of motion, but it doesn\'t seem to be severely limited.\n\n[patient]: Oh, yeah, it hurts when I move it.\n\n[doctor]: I understand. We\'ll get an X-ray to rule out any broken bones or other issues. But based on the exam, it looks like you\'ve got a contusion. How\'s your blood pressure been lately?\n\n[patient]: It\'s been a bit high, I think.\n\n[doctor]: Alright. Your blood pressure is 150/90 mmHg. We\'ll keep an eye on that. Do you have any other health issues or conditions?\n\n[patient]: Yes, I have high blood pressure and diabetes.\n\n[doctor]: Okay. How are those managed?\n\n[patient]: I take lisinopril for my blood pressure and metformin for my diabetes.\n\n[doctor]: Alright. Your blood pressure is well-controlled on the lisinopril, and it sounds like your diabetes is well-controlled too. We\'ll keep you on the metformin for now. \n\n[patient]: Great, thank you.\n\n[doctor]: You\'ll need to avoid playing lacrosse for a couple of weeks to let your elbow heal. After that, you should be fine to continue playing normally.\n\n[patient]: Okay, that\'s good to know.\n\n[doctor]: I\'ll prescribe ibuprofen 800 mg twice a day to help with the pain and swelling. You should also ice the area in 20-minute intervals, 3 times a day.\n\n[patient]: Alright, I can do that.\n\n[doctor]: That will help reduce the swelling and pain. We\'ll also order an X-ray to confirm there are no other issues. \n\n[patient]: Okay.\n\n[doctor]: You\'ll need to keep up with your dietary modifications for your blood pressure.\n\n[patient]: Yes, I\'ll keep doing that.\n\n[doctor]: Great. We\'ll also order a 